@startuml ResetPassword

title Reset Password API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Reset Password Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "m_user" as m_user
    database "t_user_reset_password" as t_user_reset_password
end box

user -> page: Request password reset
activate page
page -> api: POST v1/auth/reset-password (UTC timestamp, emailAddress over TLS)
activate api
api -> app: [**ResetPasswordCommandHandler**] Process request
activate app
    note over app, infra
        Lock order: validate -> prepare encrypted email/token/hash -> autocommit ACTIVE user lookup -> BEGIN READ
        COMMITTED -> lock the same user FOR UPDATE, rechecking ACTIVE status and email equality -> capture fresh
        server UTC now after the lock -> count history -> replace ACTIVE reset -> insert -> COMMIT -> post-commit
        email handoff -> generic 200. Derive userId only from the lookup. A lookup that finds no ACTIVE user returns
        generic 200 without BEGIN/writes. A user that becomes ineligible before the lock returns the same 200 after
        closing the read-only transaction, without counting/writing/sending.
        Execution order: validate input -> deterministic encryption and random token/hash -> routing lookup -> BEGIN
        -> locked ACTIVE user/email recheck -> fresh now/windowStart/expiredAt -> current history count -> throttle
        branch -> close old ACTIVE reset -> insert new reset with created_at = now -> COMMIT -> email handoff ->
        generic 200. Each SQL result returns to Application before branching or deriving userId/resetId.
    end note
app -> app: Generate requestId if omitted; validate UTC timestamp and email string/format/max 254
note over app, infra
    Validate mandatory timestamp as UTC and emailAddress as a non-empty, syntactically valid string of at most
    254 characters before SQL (400 E10001). Generate requestId if omitted. Accept plaintext only over TLS;
    Application applies the same deterministic encryption/representation as register/login to produce
    emailAddressBytes. Do not trim, lowercase or normalize it differently from those APIs. All SQL parameters
    are typed bound bytes/UUIDs/UTC timestamps; never interpolate input into SQL.
    Before the lookup, perform the same encryption and cryptographic preparation for every syntactically valid
    request: generate a cryptographically random 32-byte token, encode it as unpadded base64url, hash the exact
    encoded token with SHA-256 (32 bytes) as resetTokenHash. The database stores only the hash; never log/return
    the raw token, hash or email plaintext. Discard the unused in-memory secret when no row will be created.
    Apply the same configured response-latency policy to every 200 business outcome; do not deliberately return
    sooner for unknown/inactive/throttled accounts. Actual timing privacy needs runtime verification and is not
    proved by document checks.
    Only the registered address matching the encrypted lookup/locked row may receive the link; never accept a
    target userId or alternate recipient/redirect URL from the request. Build the link from the configured
    trusted reset-page URL plus the raw token. Sending is outside this spec; the handoff occurs only after the
    new row COMMIT succeeds. Do not send after rollback, for unknown/inactive users or when throttled. Email
    transport/retries/durable delivery are not defined or claimed here, as in WP4 U11; their outcome does not
    expose account existence through this HTTP response.
end note
alt Invalid timestamp or email
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Display generic operational/validation failure
else Valid input
    app -> app: emailAddressBytes = same deterministic encryption as register/login; no trimming or case change
    app -> app: Generate 32 random bytes; rawResetToken = unpadded base64url; resetTokenHash = SHA-256 exact encoded token
    alt Routing lookup timeout before BEGIN
        app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
        api -> page: Display generic operational/validation failure
    else Routing lookup failure before BEGIN
        app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
        api -> page: Display generic operational/validation failure
    else Routing lookup completes
        app -> infra: QUERY - Find the active user by email address
        infra -> m_user: QUERY - Find the active user by email address
        activate m_user
            note right of m_user
                SELECT
                    u.id as user_id
                FROM authen.m_user u
                WHERE u.email_address = '<sequence.emailAddressBytes>'
                AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
            end note
            m_user -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching userId or no row
        deactivate m_user
        infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching userId or no row
        alt No ACTIVE matching user
            app -> app: Discard unused secret; no email; apply common configured response-latency policy
            note over app, infra
                Same status-only envelope, no data/token/userId/count/refusal reason. No 401, 403, 404, 409 or 429 is added.
                Operational lookup/transaction timeout is 408 E90001; unexpected failure is generic 500 without bizCode,
                revealing no account detail. The generic success message does not certify email delivery.
                Count rows with created_at > windowStart, where windowStart = post-lock now minus 1 hour; equality is
                outside the window. Consumed/replaced/expired/history rows still count; refused attempts create no row and
                do not extend the window. Under the user lock, requests >= 3 commits no reset change and sends nothing;
                requests < 3 may issue once. Concurrent requests must reread the count after acquiring the common user lock.
                A user has at most one ACTIVE reset row (partial unique index `uq_t_user_reset_password_user_id_active`).
                Make all earlier ACTIVE reset rows of that user INACTIVE, then INSERT exactly one fresh row, in one
                transaction; zero old rows is valid. Preserve prior non-ACTIVE history and every other user. Check the
                returned new reset_id/count before success; unexpected INSERT failure/constraint failure rolls back the
                earlier closure and returns generic 500, never a new 409. Do not change password, access/refresh tokens,
                consent or authorization assignments when merely requesting a reset.
            end note
            app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 If the email address is registered, a reset link has been sent.; status only, no data
            api -> page: Display same generic acknowledgement
            page -> user: Check email if registered
        else ACTIVE matching user returned
            app -> app: userId = returned user_id; never request target user
            app -> infra: BEGIN READ COMMITTED
            note over app, infra
                Use the same fresh post-lock clock for updated_at, explicit created_at, windowStart and expiredAt = now plus
                30 minutes (configurable). Do not rely on transaction-start NOW() or default created_at after a lock wait: a
                just-issued row must be counted as new. The 30-minute lifetime begins when issued under the lock; it is
                never derived from the untrusted request timestamp. The database session and bound timestamp values use UTC.
                The common user lock serializes concurrent issuances and create-new-password. Each permitted issuance
                replaces its predecessor; only the newest remains usable and every issued row counts towards the limit, even
                if email delivery order differs. If password completion wins first, it consumes its reset before this later
                request issues a fresh link; if a new issuance wins first, the waiting completion's guarded old-token
                consumption fails. Do not extend expiry or reactivate a replaced/used row.
                The replacement transaction must COMMIT before email handoff and success. On pre-commit timeout ROLLBACK
                then 408 E90001; on other pre-commit failure ROLLBACK then generic 500. Pre-BEGIN lookup failures have no
                transaction to roll back. A lost response after commit does not undo or reuse the new token: a retry is a
                new issuance request subject to the same throttle. No post-commit email failure may roll back a committed
                row or turn the generic business outcome into an account-specific response.
            end note
            alt Transaction work completes
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the user
                infra -> m_user: QUERY - Lock the user
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        SELECT
                            u.id as user_id
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = '<sequence.userId>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND u.email_address = '<sequence.emailAddressBytes>'
                        FOR UPDATE -- every authen API locks the user row first
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return ACTIVE same-email user row or no row
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE same-email user row or no row
                alt User no longer ACTIVE or email no longer matches
                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                    app -> app: Discard unused secret; no email; apply common configured response-latency policy
                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 If the email address is registered, a reset link has been sent.; status only, no data
                    api -> page: Display same generic acknowledgement
                    page -> user: Check email if registered
                else Locked ACTIVE same-email user
                    app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now after user lock; windowStart = now minus 1 hour; expiredAt = now plus 30 minutes
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Count the requests of the last hour
                    infra -> t_user_reset_password: QUERY - Count the requests of the last hour
                    activate t_user_reset_password
                        note right of t_user_reset_password
                            SELECT
                                COUNT(rp.id) as requests
                            FROM authen.t_user_reset_password rp
                            WHERE rp.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                            AND rp.created_at > '<sequence.windowStart>' -- now minus 1 hour (configurable)
                        end note
                        t_user_reset_password -> infra: Return requests count across every reset lifecycle status
                    deactivate t_user_reset_password
                    infra -> app: Return requests count across every reset lifecycle status
                    alt requests >= 3
                        app -> infra: COMMIT
                        app -> app: Discard unused secret; no reset changes or email; apply common configured response-latency policy
                        app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 If the email address is registered, a reset link has been sent.; status only, no data
                        api -> page: Display same generic acknowledgement
                        page -> user: Check email if registered
                    else requests < 3
                        app -> infra: UPDATE - Make the old reset token INACTIVE
                        infra -> t_user_reset_password: UPDATE - Make the old reset token INACTIVE
                        activate t_user_reset_password
                            note right of t_user_reset_password
                                UPDATE authen.t_user_reset_password
                                SET
                                    updated_by = '<sequence.userId>',
                                    updated_at = '<sequence.now>',
                                    row_status = 'INACTIVE'
                                WHERE user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                                AND row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                            end note
                            t_user_reset_password -> infra: Return oldClosedCount; zero is valid
                        deactivate t_user_reset_password
                        infra -> app: Return oldClosedCount; zero is valid
                        app -> infra: INSERT - Create reset token
                        infra -> t_user_reset_password: INSERT - Create reset token
                        activate t_user_reset_password
                            note right of t_user_reset_password
                                INSERT INTO authen.t_user_reset_password (
                                    created_by,
                                    created_at,
                                    user_id,
                                    reset_token,
                                    expired_at
                                )
                                VALUES (
                                    &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.now>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.resetTokenHash>', -- SHA-256 of the token that is sent by email
                                    &#39;<sequence.expiredAt>' -- now plus 30 minutes (configurable)
                                )
                                RETURNING id as reset_id
                            end note
                            t_user_reset_password -> infra: Return new reset_id or unexpected no row
                        deactivate t_user_reset_password
                        infra -> app: Return new reset_id or unexpected no row
                        alt Exactly one new reset_id returned
                            app -> app: resetId = returned reset_id; retain raw token only in memory until post-commit handoff
                            app -> infra: COMMIT
                            infra -> app: Return committed reset replacement
                            app -> app: Request email handoff only for committed new reset; registered recipient and configured trusted reset URL
                            app -> infra: Hand off reset email after COMMIT (delivery outside this API contract)
                            infra -> app: Return handoff attempt; do not expose delivery outcome or undo commit
                            app -> app: Discard raw secret; apply common configured response-latency policy
                            app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 If the email address is registered, a reset link has been sent.; status only, no data
                            api -> page: Display same generic acknowledgement
                            page -> user: Check email if registered
                        else Unexpected zero INSERT result
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                            api -> page: Display generic operational/validation failure
                        end
                    end
                end
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Display generic operational/validation failure
            else Unexpected pre-commit failure
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Display generic operational/validation failure
            end
        end
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
